## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design streaming distinct counting under memory constraints, a common real-world need in chat pipelines. Introduces HyperLogLog beyond basic frequency sketches and checks ability to reason about merging across shards.

## Key Concepts
- HyperLogLog for cardinality estimation
- Memory-constant sketch with m registers and 5–6 bits per register
- Per-element update and merge operations (max per register)
- Relative error ~1.04/√m; small-bias corrections for tiny cardinalities
- Trade-offs: m vs accuracy vs memory; cross-shard merging

## Code Example
```javascript
function updateHLL(M, xHash64) {
  const p = M.length ? Math.log2(M.length) : 0;
  const i = xHash64 >>> (64 - p);
  const w = (xHash64 << p) >>> 0;
  const v = 1 + Math.clz32(~w); // rough trailing zeros proxy
  M[i] = Math.max(M[i], v);
}

function estimateCardinality(M) {
  const m = M.length;
  const sum = M.reduce((acc, x) => acc + Math.pow(2, -x), 0);
  const alpha = (m === 16) ? 0.673 : (m === 32) ? 0.697 : (m === 64) ? 0.709 : 0.721;
  return (alpha * m * m) / sum;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Explores practical dynamic approximate all-pairs shortest paths (APSP) with shared structure; tests understanding of trade-offs between update costs and query time in batch-dynamic settings.

## Key Concepts
- Batch-dynamic graphs with nonnegative edge weights
- Hub-based distance sketches for approximate APSP
- Amortized analysis across multiple query pairs
- Trade-offs between approximation accuracy ε and computational efficiency
- Incremental shortest path algorithms

## Code Example
```javascript
// Hub-based distance approximation: dist(u,v) ≈ min_h∈H [dist(u,h) + dist(h,v)]

class HubBasedAPSP {
  constructor(graph, epsilon) {
    this.k = Math.ceil((1/epsilon) * Math.log(graph.n));
    this.hubs = this.selectHubs(graph);
    this.distances = new Map(); // hub -> vertex distances
  }

  updateBatch(edges) {
    for (const hub of this.hubs) {
      this.distances.set(hub, this.incrementalDijkstra(hub, edges));
    }
  }

  query(u, v) {
    let minDist = Infinity;
    for (const hub of this.hubs) {
      const dist = this.distances.get(hub).get(u) + 
                   this.distances.get(hub).get(v);
      minDist = Math.min(minDist, dist);
    }
    return minDist;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
